  "term": "flashbulb memory",
  "definition": "Flashbulb memory is a type of autobiographical memory marked by vivid, long-lasting recall of the personal circumstances in which someone learned important news or experienced a public event. It includes rich self-related details and can help shape how people remember that event.",
